From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0428-area-change-01-release-obsolete-scratch.patch

Source: 0428-area-change-01-release-obsolete-scratch.patch
EDEN_AREA_CHANGE_SCRATCH_RELEASE=1 releases obsolete scratch before allocating
its larger replacement. Unset or any other value preserves the existing path.
A failed replacement leaves an empty buffer with zero size and capacity.
This reduces overlapping allocations during loading; it is not a proven fix
for run149's unidentified 3316524576-byte host request.

Assisted-by: OpenAI Codex (analysis, patch draft and local validation)

diff --git a/src/common/scratch_buffer.h b/src/common/scratch_buffer.h
index fcbd1a22c9..4ba2516497 100644
--- a/src/common/scratch_buffer.h
+++ b/src/common/scratch_buffer.h
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 
 #include <iterator>
 #include <cstring>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <memory>
 
 namespace Common {
@@ -76,8 +77,17 @@ public:
     /// The previously held data will be destroyed if a reallocation occurs.
     void resize_destructive(size_type size) {
         if (size > buffer_capacity) {
-            // Allocate first: a caller that catches the failure must not be left with the new
-            // capacity on the old, smaller buffer, or the next resize writes past its end.
+            static const bool release_before_growth = [] {
+                const char* value = std::getenv("EDEN_AREA_CHANGE_SCRATCH_RELEASE");
+                return value != nullptr && value[0] == '1' && value[1] == '\0';
+            }();
+            // Area transitions can grow scratch while the old area's memory is still held.
+            // Destructive growth needs none of these bytes; release() also resets the sizes
+            // if the replacement allocation fails.
+            if (release_before_growth) {
+                release();
+            }
+            // Publish the new capacity only after allocation succeeds.
             buffer = std::make_unique_for_overwrite<T[]>(size);
             buffer_capacity = size;
         }
